Forge: this instance works with GitLab, not GitHub. Wherever these rules or the prompt name a `gh` command or GitHub vocabulary, use the GitLab equivalent from this section; use `glab`, never `gh`.
- Vocabulary: a pull request is a merge request, checks are pipelines, a PR review is a merge request approval or note, the repository is a project.
- Refs: `#N` is an issue, `!N` is a merge request, `<namespace>/<project>#N` and `<namespace>/<project>!N` name an issue or merge request in another project. A GitHub-style `#N` never means a merge request here.
- Commands (GitHub → GitLab):

| GitHub                                  | GitLab                                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `gh issue view <N>`                     | `glab issue view <N>`                                                       |
| `gh issue list`                         | `glab issue list`                                                           |
| `gh issue create`                       | `glab issue create`                                                         |
| `gh pr view <N>`                        | `glab mr view <N>`                                                          |
| `gh pr view <N> --comments`             | `glab mr view <N> --comments`                                               |
| `gh pr diff <N>`                        | `glab mr diff <N>`                                                          |
| `gh pr checks <N>`                      | `glab ci status` (the pipeline of the current branch)                       |
| `gh pr comment <N>`                     | `glab mr note <N> -m "…"`                                                   |
| `gh pr review <N> --approve`            | `glab mr approve <N>`                                                       |
| `gh api <endpoint>`                     | `glab api <endpoint>` (REST v4, for example `projects/:fullpath/merge_requests/<N>`) |

- `-R <owner/repo>` becomes `-R <namespace>/<project>`.
